# Content Rules

## Never Invent Content

Until real content exists from the project fact sheets:

- **Never invent clients** — no fake company names
- **Never invent figures** — no made-up stats, metrics, results, dates
- **Never invent credits** — no fake agency names, awards, press mentions
- **Never invent logos** — no placeholder brand marks
- **Never invent case details** — no fake stack, tech, or outcomes

## Use Clear Placeholders

Every content slot without real data must be a **clearly marked placeholder**:

```
CASO PENDIENTE
CLIENTE PENDIENTE  
CRÉDITO PENDIENTE
CIFRA PENDIENTE
MEDIA PENDIENTE
```

Never use realistic-looking sample cases like "Acme Corp" or "Project X" that could be mistaken for real work.

## Placeholder Styling

- Use the same typography role the final content will use
- Add `text-[var(--nml-color-text-secondary)]` for visual distinction
- In code, mark with comments: `{/* PLACEHOLDER: awaiting fact sheet */}`

## Real Data Sources

Real content comes only from:
- Project fact sheets (verified case data)
- Client-approved materials
- Confirmed press/awards with citations

A figure only appears if it has a source in the fact sheet and indicates whether it's first-party or third-party data.

## Media Placeholders

For images/video without rights or files yet:
- Show a gray placeholder box (#2a2a2a for hero, #f2f2f2 elsewhere)
- Include label: "Fotograma real del caso · pendiente de derechos"
- Never use stock photos or generated images as stand-ins
